WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.920
By the time "Sons of Anarchy" finished&nbsp;
its seven-season-long ride back in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.240
the FX show had become one of the&nbsp;
must-see crime dramas of its time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.800
It doesn't have the nuance achieved by other&nbsp;
critically acclaimed shows like "The Wire"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.440
or "Breaking Bad," but the series' lovable&nbsp;
band of rogues is no less entertaining.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:25.120
"Sons of Anarchy" follows Jax Teller, played by&nbsp;
Charlie Hunnam, as he goes through an existential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.960
crisis. He discovers that his long-dead father&nbsp;
didn't want the Sons of Anarchy Motorcycle Club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.600
Redwood Original, to be a criminal&nbsp;
enterprise funded by drugs and gun-running.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.560
As communicated posthumously through&nbsp;
a discovered manuscript, John Teller's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.800
high-minded ideals and peaceful vision for&nbsp;
SAMCRO basically upends his son's entire world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.000
Jax is suddenly pulled between his duty to&nbsp;
his brothers' conflicts with his father's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.920
undeclared vision, and what&nbsp;
Jax himself knows to be right.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.720
"Sons of Anarchy" is a grimy and&nbsp;
unrelenting view of the criminal underworld,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.240
but its roguish characters are&nbsp;
somewhat charming. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:10.560
they do dish out brutal punishments to anyone who&nbsp;
crosses them. Notably, the series was envisioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:16.400
as a modern-day retelling of Shakespeare's&nbsp;
"Hamlet." Jax is the indecisive Danish prince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.040
and his father's posthumous words are&nbsp;
a kind of reimagined paternal ghost.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.800
"I am thy father's spirit."

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:31.600
The central conflict between Jax, Clay, played&nbsp;
by Ron Perlman, and Gemma, played by Katey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:38.320
Sagal even mirrors the conflict between Hamlet,&nbsp;
Claudius, and Gertrude from the Elizabethan play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:44.000
Shakespeare's original story is pretty grim in&nbsp;
its own right, but "Sons of Anarchy" creator Kurt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.480
Sutter took the FX series to some dark places&nbsp;
even the bard wasn't willing to conjure. Gore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.280
death, and torture are splattered&nbsp;
across nearly every single season.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.960
Since there are so many&nbsp;
deaths throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.400
some moments get lost in the sea of blood.&nbsp;
However, there's one particular death from "Sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.360
of Anarchy" that stands above the rest because&nbsp;
of the emotional weight that comes with it.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:15.600
The death of Harry "Opie" Winston, played by Ryan&nbsp;
Hurst, during one of the Sons' brief stints behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:23.120
bars in Season 5 is emotionally devastating, and&nbsp;
many fans are still reeling from the loss. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.720
Gemma killing Tara Knowles, played by Maggie&nbsp;
Siff, in Season 6 is horrific. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.000
the reason Opie's death hits harder is&nbsp;
because it's the last self-destructive step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.760
on a long journey into despair that begins&nbsp;
after Opie loses his wife in Season 1.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.920
He's ultimately killed in retaliation&nbsp;
for the death of the daughter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.440
Harold Perrineau's character, Damon Pope.&nbsp;
His daughter was accidentally killed by Tig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.640
played by Kim Coates, when attacking another&nbsp;
club. Though he gets to play the hero and save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:00.800
his brothers through self-sacrifice, Opie's final&nbsp;
act is as much an escape for him as anything else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.880
He's running away from a life&nbsp;
he'd long given up living.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.800
Opie volunteers to fight in prison&nbsp;
knowing he's going to be killed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:14.800
Jax, Tig, and Chibs, played by Tommy Flanagan,&nbsp;
watch on in horror as two other inmates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.560
mercilessly beat Opie to death with a pipe. To&nbsp;
make matters even more galling, the whole thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.320
is facilitated by a corrections officer who's&nbsp;
presumably in Pope's pocket. That bond between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.600
Opie and the brothers he saves is what makes&nbsp;
it the most impactful death in the series.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.080
Rolling Stone voted it the 4th best&nbsp;
moment in "Sons of Anarchy" overall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.600
and it was exceeded only by sentimental scenes.&nbsp;
No other death scene — even those involving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.520
main characters — comes close. Entertainment&nbsp;
Weekly also ranked Opie's death 4th in the 50&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:53.760
most shocking moments of the series, and his death&nbsp;
nabbed the top spot in a similar list at Goliath.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.600
But even after Opie's gruesome slaying, "Sons&nbsp;
of Anarchy" is clearly a series that continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:05.280
to loom large in the imaginations of its fans.&nbsp;
The show's enduring impact is enough to fuel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.800
continued discussions on social media, even&nbsp;
years after the series took its final bow.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.840
The cast were equally heartbroken over&nbsp;
Opie's death. As a way of saying goodbye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.440
they all shaved Hurst's beard with a samurai&nbsp;
sword. Hunnam told Entertainment Weekly,

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.280
"I started crying, and then [Mark]&nbsp;
Boone started crying. By the end of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.840
it was the catharsis that&nbsp;
we'd all hoped it would be."

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.640
So R.I.P., Opie Winston. Don't&nbsp;
cry too hard about it, though.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.080
Ryan Hurst landed a sweet gig&nbsp;
playing Beta on "The Walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.200
Dead" after departing "Sons of Anarchy,"&nbsp;
and for that, we are eternally grateful.

